      <workList xml:id="idm114">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e232229">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_3637d229">B3:Coll.001</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="de">D. Balthasar Münters erste Sammlung geistlicher Lieder</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_119a14c6">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="_22">Balthasar Münter</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_23_0">
               <date isodate="1773" xml:id="date_ad0e40a7">1773</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_7b3f83f6">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_23_0">
               <p xml:id="idm126">
                  <persName xml:id="idm127" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Balthasar Münter</persName> had been employed as preacher for the German congregation at the St Petri Church in Copenhagen since 1765. As <persName xml:id="idm128" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Heinrich Wilhelm von Gerstenberg</persName>, also Münter's home was renowned for hosting a circle of German intellectuals living in Copenhagen; among the participants were <persName xml:id="idm129" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Friedrich Gottlieb Klopstock</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm130" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Andreas Cramer</persName>, Gerstenberg and probably also Scheibe. In 1773, Münter published a collection of so-called sacred songs (‘geistliche Lieder’), of which many must rather be termed chorales. Münter gave Scheibe a fair copy of the texts and Scheibe wrote twelve of the songs and chorales in the volume. The collection also includes settings by <persName xml:id="idm131" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Carl Philipp Emanuel Bach</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm132" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Adam Hiller</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm133" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Adolph Carl Kunzen</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm134" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Heinrich Rolle</persName> and <persName xml:id="idm135" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Christoph Friedrich Bach</persName>.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_18817a24">
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
               <language xml:id="de">German</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="listBibl_a7d188dd-3bc3-4f0e-815d-fc1d5c07e95f276">
